regexec.c: the regset first-byte test also covers anchored regexes

Patch 0007 tested the first byte inline only for regexes at distance 0
with no anchor (reg->anchor == 0). That condition is not needed:
forward_search() reads dist_min, dist_max, sub_anchor and the optimize
data, never reg->anchor, so for an anchored regex it reports the same
candidates in the same order as the inline test. Whether the anchor
holds is still decided where it was: match_at() checks \G, \A and
look-behind, and the ANCR_ANYCHAR_INF test before each try still runs.
Grammars use \G and look-behind a lot (TypeScript's keywords start with
(?<![_$[:alnum:]])), so many more regexes now skip forward_search().

See rust/vendor/README.md.

diff --git a/oniguruma/src/regexec.c b/oniguruma/src/regexec.c
